<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohamed Nasheed</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1967</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohamed Nasheed is a Maldivian politician who became the country's first democratically elected president in 2008, under a new multiparty constitution, ending the thirty-year rule of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maumoon-abdul-gayoom">Maumoon Abdul Gayoom</a>. He gained international attention for his climate campaigning on behalf of low-lying states. He resigned under pressure in 2012, was later imprisoned, and served as speaker of parliament from 2019 to 2023.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mohamed-nasheed.jpg" alt="Mohamed Nasheed" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The President's Office · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_Mohamed_Nasheed_2022.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
